{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/942394-aiming-for-specific-parts","id":942394,"title":"Aiming for specific parts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-02T18:57:30-07:00","id":942394,"title":"Aiming for specific parts","content":"Hello, I was discussing with a friend aiming and ignoring armor.<br /> <br /> In the aim bit it states 'attacking a specific body part has its benefits. In addition to ignoring armor, strikes to limbs and the head can have added effects' <br /> <br /> Now in armor it says that the cover is torso legs arms. So question is if someone has armor that covers torso legs arms can you aim for hand and ignore armor as hand and arm are -4 and -2 respectively two separate parts to aim at. <br /> <br /> Same for the eyes if someone is wearing plate which states torso arms legs no helmets I can see but let's say they have one can you aim for the slit in the visor at -5 going for eyes to ignore armor or is that impossible as my friend thinks you can never get through the slit with anything and no one can aim through it as its too small. I am of the impression you can aim for the eyes and get past the plate armor.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts or links to rulings somewhere would be great thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12176-theboydante","name":"TheBoyDante","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T19:03:29-07:00","id":942398,"title":"","content":"*Helmets found, hidden nicely as coverage under armor \ud83d\udc4d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12176-theboydante","name":"TheBoyDante","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T19:06:41-07:00","id":942400,"title":"","content":"Correction I said most weapons wouldn't fit through the slit. Something like a shiv or spike could but most weapons were thicker than the eye slits of helmets so even aiming for the eye means having to force past the metal helmets toughness. Along with it being a smaller target than the normal eye, and your angle of approach being limited to one specific direction of approach because of helmet design and the person moving around.<br /> <br /> And also as mentioned for background information every suit of full plate armor has gauntlets which cover the hand. Either the coverage is not specific enough, or it refers to a general coverage of the entire location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T19:09:04-07:00","id":942402,"title":"","content":"Hence the -5 penalty.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12176-theboydante","name":"TheBoyDante","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T19:49:44-07:00","id":942427,"title":"","content":"The thing is, it's a -5 penalty to aim for the eyes, even if they aren't wearing a helmet. So I might increase that penalty a bit if you are aiming for the eyes through the slit in a helmet's visor.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, not many people wear visored helmets these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T20:23:15-07:00","id":942443,"title":"","content":"Riot helmets usually have a plastic visor, making it much harder to make a called shot around it, but not impossible (since you can still come up underneath most versions of it instead of through an eye-slit.<br /> <br /> But yeah, you can ignore armor with a called shot, but thankfully with the boosted Defense of 2e, it's actually a meaningful choice most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T00:32:19-07:00","id":942550,"title":"","content":"If still aiming for a protected body part: a good rule of thumb for attacks around helmets/visors/armor ist to add the whole armor rating as a penalty to the roll. This usually adds some high risk, high reward mechanics. The attack should of course make sense in some way, so that you have a weapon specifically useful for this like the mentioned shiv. Forcing a baseball bat in between the slit of a visor and a helmet, would be kind of stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T12:44:45-07:00","id":943787,"title":"","content":"In some cases, you might actually lose more damage by accepting accuracy penalty than you would lose to armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}